Add the missing Drupal\Core\Url import to WidgetPluginBase.

WidgetPluginBase::build() calls `new Url(...)` when rebuilding a facet whose
result URL is routed to facets.block.ajax, but the class is never imported, so
PHP resolves it as Drupal\facets\Widget\Url and fatals with:

  Class "Drupal\facets\Widget\Url" not found

This only surfaces on /facets-block-ajax requests for facets sourced from a
views block, which is why it does not appear on normal page loads.

Present in 2.0.10 and on 2.0.x HEAD.

diff --git a/src/Widget/WidgetPluginBase.php b/src/Widget/WidgetPluginBase.php
--- a/src/Widget/WidgetPluginBase.php
+++ b/src/Widget/WidgetPluginBase.php
@@ -6,7 +6,8 @@
 use Drupal\Component\Utility\NestedArray;
 use Drupal\Core\Form\FormStateInterface;
 use Drupal\Core\Link;
 use Drupal\Core\Plugin\PluginBase;
+use Drupal\Core\Url;
 use Drupal\facets\FacetInterface;
 use Drupal\facets\Result\Result;
 use Drupal\facets\Result\ResultInterface;
